Links to an article on mediawiki.org (https://www.mediawiki.org/).

Usage:

* {{ml|link target on MediaWikiWiki}}
* {{ml|link target on MediaWikiWiki|label}}

The English source pages no longer use this. They spell the link out as an external
link with the URL inside a <tvar>, so the link carries the external-link marker its
target deserves and a translator never retypes the URL:

* [<tvar name="1">https://www.mediawiki.org/wiki/Special:MyLanguage/Help:Templates</tvar> Templates]

The template stays for the translations that still transclude it.
